{"title":"2021 GMC 12B Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive perfect square integer, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37be22cfff67e93c85071fbef5c965ae7d212ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$min(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is also an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af6b94dcef4d49f4aa4b0d7f97a116bdb0506d08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~9 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~12 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~30 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~36 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the perfect square. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dacad67efea670e3ac20a8a4c0c75159fb1ac01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\dfrac{10}3 s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the first perfect square that is divisble by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c569d583336516cd11ef4331cedf28aba2d3ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 9$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a28f05b453604191929b7ba5452dfa8aea2479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\dfrac{10}3s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4d3b901dd84d35720444889d7dc1c1f61a3d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~pineconee\n</p>